<!-- ================= PHILOSOPHY ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="sh-top"><span class="sec-no">(03)</span><span>WHY FOLDERGRAM</span><span class="sh-rule"></span></div>
      <h2>Less digging. <em class="grad">More remembering.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">Your photo archive already has a home. Foldergram gives it a more enjoyable way to be explored, without asking you to reorganize your life around another photo library.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="terms">
      <div class="term bad rv">
        <div class="t-bar"><span class="dot"></span>your photos, as folders</div>
        <div class="t-body">
<span class="tline" style="--d:.05s">~/photos/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.5s">├── summer-road-trip/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.95s">├── old-phone-backup/</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.4s">└── random-memories/</span>
<span class="tline t-dim" style="--d:1.85s">open a folder → open a photo → go back</span>
<span class="tline t-dim" style="--d:2.3s">organized, but easy to forget</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="term good rv" style="--d:.1s">
        <div class="t-bar"><span class="dot"></span>your photos, in Foldergram</div>
        <div class="t-body">
<span class="tline">~/photos/ → <span class="t-pr">your personal feed</span></span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.5s">your folders → individual profiles</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:.95s">your videos → Reels</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.4s">old favorites → Rediscover</span>
<span class="tline" style="--d:1.85s">same library, <span class="t-pr">a new way to browse</span></span>
<span class="tline t-dim" style="--d:2.3s">original files stay where they are</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="pull rv"><span class="pull-line">“You didn't save those memories to forget them.</span><span class="pull-line grad">Give your memories a way back into your day.”</span></blockquote>
    <div class="why-principles">
      <article class="why-principle">
        <h3>Your files, your structure.</h3>
        <p>Keep the folders and storage you already use. Foldergram indexes your media in place, storing its database and generated previews separately. It complements your file manager rather than replacing it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="why-principle">
        <h3>Your server, your privacy.</h3>
        <p>Run Foldergram on hardware you control. Local browsing needs no cloud account or remote media service, and you decide how your gallery is accessible.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="why-principle">
        <h3>Your memories, not a social network.</h3>
        <p>Enjoy the familiar experience of a social feed without comments, messaging or a platform competing for your attention. It's a space for the moments you've already saved.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
